reagent-name-morphine = morphine
reagent-desc-morphine = A potent analgesic for awake surgery. Suppresses surgical pain reactions, with the effect lasting up to 30 seconds after the reagent stops acting. Causes drowsiness. A bloodstream concentration of 16 units or more causes suffocation. Does not heal injuries or replace patient consent.
ent-ChemistryBottleMorphine = morphine bottle
    .desc = An analgesic for surgery. Causes drowsiness; an overdose depresses breathing.
    .suffix = Morphine
ent-StatusEffectSurgicalAnalgesia = surgical analgesia
    .desc = Temporarily suppresses pain reactions during surgery.
